cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use BioPilot CLI in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "BioPilot CLI: version-aware and project-aware terminal autocompletion for bioinformatics"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "BioPilot CLI contributors"
version: 1.1.4
date-released: 2026-11-08
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DEDJIABDOUL/biopilot-cli"
abstract: >-
  BioPilot CLI suggests, while a command is typed, the options, files and values
  that fit bioinformatics tools such as fastp, samtools, bwa or minimap2, as they
  are actually installed in the active environment (conda, mamba), and for the
  project being worked on (file formats, read pairs, reference indexes). It runs
  locally, without network access or telemetry.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - command line
  - autocompletion
  - shell
  - conda
  - reproducibility
